# Lesson 2, from the Lesson 2 bidding exercise 3e (partner opens 1S).
title: Partner opens 1♠: respond 2NT
id: L02-17
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.3, 2.6
student: S
board: 17
dealer: N
vulnerable: none

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  AQ864  Q2     KJ4    Q83
  E  K532   T953   763    J4
  S  J7     AK64   QT5    K975
  W  T9     J87    A982   AT62

auction:
  N 1S     = 13+ points, at least four spades
  E Pass
  S 2NT*   = 12-14 points, balanced, no spade support
     key: 13 HCP, balanced, and only two spades. Respond 2NT.
     not 2S: 2♠ shows 6-9 with support. Did you count 13?
     not 3S: 3♠ needs four spades. You have two.
     not 2H: To bid hearts at the two level you need five of them.
     not *: With a balanced 12-14 and no spade support, which response fits?
  W Pass
  N 3NT    = Game
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = Partner has chosen the game
     key: Partner has bid game. Pass.
     not *: Partner has bid game. Is there anything left to say?
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Your 2NT showed a balanced 12-14 without spade support. Partner, with
  13+ of her own, knew your side had 25 and bid game. You are declarer,
  because you bid no-trump first, and so West will lead to the first
  trick.

planning:
  remind: What is the contract? How many tricks do you need?

play:
  1   W D2  N D4  E D3  S DT
  2   S SJ  W ST  N S4  E SK
      note: The plan: set up the spades, then take your hearts and diamonds and a club. Start with your ♠J.
  3   E D7  S D5  W DA  N DJ
  4   W D8  N DK  E D6  S DQ
  5   N SQ  E S2  S S7  W S9
      note: Now run the spades.
  6   N SA  E S3  S H4  W C6
      note: Keep going.
  7   N S8  E S5  S C5  W H7
      note: Dummy's spades are all winners.
  8   N S6  E H3  S C7  W C2
      note: The last spade.
  9   N C3  E C4  S CK  W CA
      note: Lead a club toward your ♣K.
  10  W D9  N C8  E H5  S H6
      note: West cashes the last diamond.
  11  W CT  N CQ  E CJ  S C9
      note: Dummy's ♣Q wins.
  12  N H2  E H9  S HK  W H8
      note: Now the hearts: a heart to your ♥K.
  13  S HA  W HJ  N HQ  E HT
      note: 9 tricks: 3NT made.

play recap:
  The plan: set up the spades, then take your hearts, diamonds and a club.

  3NT made. Partner's five spades turned into four tricks once the king
  was gone.
